%N A160687 Primes p such that p^2-2, p^4-2, p^6-2, p^8-2 and p^10-2 are all prime.
%C A160687 p=15912460901 is in this sequence and p^12-2 is also prime.
%C A160687 All terms are == +-1 (mod 7): the squares modulo 7 are 0, 1, 2, 4, and if p^2 == 2 or 4 (mod 7), then p^2 - 2 or p^4 - 2 is divisible by 7; and p = 7 fails since 7^6 - 2 is composite. a(122) > 10^11. - _Pierre Colmant_, Nov 01 2026
%H A160687 Pierre Colmant, <a href="/A160687/b160687.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..121</a> (first 53 terms from Dmitry Kamenetsky)
%e A160687 1068367 is a term: 1068367^2 - 2, 1068367^4 - 2, 1068367^6 - 2, 1068367^8 - 2 and 1068367^10 - 2 are all prime (the last one has 61 digits). - _Pierre Colmant_, Nov 01 2026
%o A160687 (Python)
%o A160687 from sympy import isprime
%o A160687 def ok(p): return isprime(p) and all(isprime(p**(2*j)-2) for j in range(1, 6))
